{{also|VOX|VOx}}
==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|la|wekʷ}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*wōks}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*wṓkʷs||speech, voice}} (with stem ''vōc-'' for ''voqu-'' from the nominative case), an [[o-grade]] [[root noun]] of {{m|ine-pro|*wekʷ-||to speak}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|sc=Deva|वाच्|tr=vā́c}} and {{cog|grc|ὄψ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=yes|vōx}}
* {{audio|la-cls-vox.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|vōx|vōcis|f|third}}

# [[voice]]
# [[accent]]
# [[speech]], [[remark]], [[expression]], (turn of) [[phrase]]
# [[word]]
# {{lb|la|grammar}} [[voice]]; indicating the relation of the subject of the verb to the action which the verb expresses

